<!-- ================= III ================= -->
<section id="iii">
  <div class="numeral">III</div>
  <h2>The temple of elaboration</h2>
  <p class="intro">Honcho dreams differently from the others: it keeps the stated facts and builds inferences on top of them, each tied to the facts that hold it up. Read from the source code (plastic-labs/honcho, commit cb8ab1a).</p>
  <div class="marble temple-box" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="temple-fig">
    <img src="/posts/images/ai-memory-dreaming/temple.webp" width="1614" height="769" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Illustration of Honcho's AI memory store as a Greek temple: columns are facts stated in sessions, gold beams are deductions made while dreaming, the pediment is an inferred pattern, and a broken column is a soft-deleted fact">
    <svg viewBox="0 -110 1614 1030" role="img" aria-label="Honcho's memory as a temple. Columns are explicit facts written during sessions. Gold beams across columns are deductive observations written while dreaming. The blue pediment is an inductive observation resting on the two facts that support it. The broken column is a soft-deleted fact.">
      <!-- induction: the pediment over columns 1 and 2 -->
      <text x="316" y="-48" text-anchor="middle" class="lbl-i" font-size="26">inductive, low confidence, 2 sources</text>
      <text x="316" y="142" text-anchor="middle" class="cap" font-size="25" fill="#2a3550">PREFERS PYTHON</text>
      <!-- deductions: the gold beams -->
      <text x="942" y="62" text-anchor="middle" class="lbl-i" font-size="26">deductive, from s4</text>
      <text x="942" y="100" text-anchor="middle" class="lbl" font-size="32">works in healthcare</text>
      <text x="1314" y="62" text-anchor="middle" class="lbl-i" font-size="26">deductive update, from s3 and s6</text>
      <text x="1314" y="100" text-anchor="middle" class="lbl" font-size="32">meeting is Thursday</text>
      <!-- the update still points at the fact it replaced -->
      <line x1="1222" y1="190" x2="1222" y2="452" stroke="#a8843f" stroke-width="3" stroke-dasharray="10 8"/>
      <text x="1240" y="300" class="lbl-i" font-size="26">premise link to a</text>
      <text x="1240" y="332" class="lbl-i" font-size="26">soft-deleted fact</text>
      <g id="plaques"></g>
    </svg>
    </div>
    <div class="temple-legend">
      <span><i class="key" style="background:#f6f1e6"></i>Column: a fact said in a session</span>
      <span><i class="key" style="background:#ead79f;border-color:#a8843f"></i>Beam: a deduction, made while dreaming</span>
      <span><i class="key" style="background:#c6d8ee;border-color:#5f86b8"></i>Pediment: a pattern, made while dreaming</span>
      <span><i class="key" style="background:transparent;border-style:dashed"></i>Ruin: deleted, but the row is kept</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="intro" style="margin-top:16px">When the store has gained 50 new explicit facts, the user has been idle for an hour, and 8 hours have passed since the last dream, a deduction agent (up to 12 tool steps) looks for updates, implications and contradictions and may delete outdated facts. Then an induction agent (up to 10 steps) writes patterns, preferences and personality traits; its prompt says "think like a psychologist". Every inference must cite the IDs of the facts it rests on; invented IDs are discarded. At answer time, the reading agent is told to check an inference's premises before trusting it.</p>
</section>

<div class="rule"></div>

<!-- ================= IV ================= -->
<section id="iv">
  <div class="numeral">IV</div>
  <h2>Six houses that dream</h2>
  <p class="intro">The six fall into two families. <em>Curation</em> rewrites memory into a cleaner version of itself; five of the six work this way. <em>Elaboration</em> keeps the stated facts and builds inferences on top of them; only Honcho does. Across both, the designs differ most in what protects memory from a bad night.</p>
  <div class="marble houses-box" style="margin-top:20px">
    <table class="houses">
      <caption class="vh">How Honcho, ChatGPT, Anthropic, Devin, OpenClaw and Letta implement dreaming, as of 8 October 2026</caption>
      <colgroup><col class="sys"><col><col><col><col><col></colgroup>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">System</th><th scope="col">Day writer</th><th scope="col">When it dreams</th><th scope="col">What the dream does</th><th scope="col">Where it writes</th><th scope="col">Safeguards</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row"><a class="emblem-link" href="https://honcho.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Honcho website"><svg class="emblem" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><polygon points="6,24 32,8 58,24" fill="#c6d8ee" stroke="#5f86b8"/><rect x="8" y="24" width="48" height="5" fill="#ead79f" stroke="#a8843f"/><g fill="#f6f1e6" stroke="#b6aa92"><rect x="12" y="29" width="6" height="22"/><rect x="29" y="29" width="6" height="22"/><rect x="46" y="29" width="6" height="22"/></g><rect x="6" y="51" width="52" height="5" fill="#f6f1e6" stroke="#b6aa92"/></svg></a><span class="name">Honcho</span><span class="kind">ELABORATION</span></th><td data-label="Day writer">One LLM call per message batch extracts atomic facts about the target peer.</td><td data-label="When it dreams">50 new facts, 60 min idle, 8 h since the last dream (defaults).</td><td data-label="What the dream does">Deduction: updates, implications, contradictions, deletes outdated facts. Induction: patterns, preferences, traits from 2+ facts.</td><td data-label="Where it writes">Same store, new rows tagged deductive, inductive, contradiction.</td><td data-label="Safeguards">Required premise IDs; soft deletes; reader told to check premises.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><a class="emblem-link" href="https://openai.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="OpenAI website"><svg class="emblem" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><g fill="#f6f1e6" stroke="#b6aa92"><rect x="6" y="10" width="18" height="10"/><rect x="6" y="27" width="18" height="10"/><rect x="6" y="44" width="18" height="10"/></g><path d="M24 15 L34 28 M24 32 L34 32 M24 49 L34 36" stroke="#a8843f" fill="none"/><rect x="34" y="18" width="24" height="28" fill="#fffaf0" stroke="#a8843f"/><g stroke="#a8843f"><line x1="38" y1="25" x2="54" y2="25"/><line x1="38" y1="31" x2="54" y2="31"/><line x1="38" y1="37" x2="49" y2="37"/></g></svg></a><span class="name">ChatGPT</span><span class="kind">CURATION</span></th><td data-label="Day writer">Saved memories, written during the chat on strong cues such as "remember I'm traveling to Singapore in July".</td><td data-label="When it dreams">Continually, in the background; no schedule is published. First version April 2025; the current one, "Dreaming V3", from June 2026.</td><td data-label="What the dream does">Learns from many conversations and synthesizes a memory state; revises entries as time passes, so "going to Singapore in July" becomes "went to Singapore in July 2026".</td><td data-label="Where it writes">A synthesized memory, shown to the user as a summary. Saved memories are stored separately.</td><td data-label="Safeguards">The user can correct the summary, mark a topic "Don't mention this again", or delete it. Temporary chats never create memories.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><a class="emblem-link" href="https://www.anthropic.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Anthropic website"><svg class="emblem" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="6" y="14" width="22" height="36" fill="#f6f1e6" stroke="#b6aa92"/><rect x="36" y="14" width="22" height="36" fill="#fffaf0" stroke="#a8843f"/><g stroke="#b6aa92"><line x1="10" y1="22" x2="24" y2="22"/><line x1="10" y1="28" x2="24" y2="28"/><line x1="10" y1="34" x2="24" y2="34"/><line x1="10" y1="40" x2="20" y2="40"/></g><g stroke="#a8843f"><line x1="40" y1="22" x2="54" y2="22"/><line x1="40" y1="28" x2="54" y2="28"/><line x1="40" y1="34" x2="50" y2="34"/></g><path d="M29 32 L35 32 M32 29 L35 32 L32 35" stroke="#a8843f" fill="none"/></svg></a><span class="name">Anthropic</span><span class="kind">CURATION</span></th><td data-label="Day writer">The agent edits files in a mounted memory store with its file tools; every change is versioned.</td><td data-label="When it dreams">The launch post calls it "a scheduled process"; the API docs show only an on-demand call.</td><td data-label="What the dream does">Reads one store and 1–100 sessions; merges duplicates, replaces stale or contradicted entries, adds "new insights". Optional steering text.</td><td data-label="Where it writes">A new, separate store. The input is never modified.</td><td data-label="Safeguards">A person decides whether to use the copy; the dream's own session can be streamed and is kept.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><a class="emblem-link" href="https://devin.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Devin website"><svg class="emblem" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="12" y="8" width="40" height="48" fill="#f6f1e6" stroke="#b6aa92"/><g stroke="#8a7a5c"><line x1="18" y1="18" x2="46" y2="18"/><line x1="18" y1="26" x2="46" y2="26"/><line x1="18" y1="34" x2="40" y2="34"/></g><line x1="18" y1="42" x2="44" y2="42" stroke="#b0503a" stroke-dasharray="2 3" opacity=".6"/><circle cx="48" cy="48" r="7" fill="none" stroke="#a8843f"/><path d="M48 44 L48 48 L51 50" stroke="#a8843f" fill="none"/></svg></a><span class="name">Devin</span><span class="kind">CURATION</span></th><td data-label="Day writer">On corrections, preferences and reusable findings, edits a note; one-line bullets that link to their session; saved as git commits.</td><td data-label="When it dreams">About once a day when you have been using Devin.</td><td data-label="What the dream does">Merges overlapping notes, drops transient details, deletes notes no session has used, adds lessons missed during the work, reorganizes the index.</td><td data-label="Where it writes">In place, in a git repo of markdown files.</td><td data-label="Safeguards">The app lists each dream and what it changed; source links and explicit preferences kept.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><a class="emblem-link" href="https://openclaw.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="OpenClaw website"><svg class="emblem" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><g fill="none" stroke="#a8843f" stroke-width="2"><path d="M6 54 V30 A6 6 0 0 1 18 30 V54"/><path d="M26 54 V30 A6 6 0 0 1 38 30 V54"/><path d="M46 54 V30 A6 6 0 0 1 58 30 V54"/></g><rect x="4" y="18" width="56" height="6" fill="#f6f1e6" stroke="#b6aa92"/><rect x="4" y="54" width="56" height="4" fill="#f6f1e6" stroke="#b6aa92"/></svg></a><span class="name">OpenClaw</span><span class="kind">CURATION, GATED</span></th><td data-label="Day writer">The agent writes daily notes; recall of each snippet is recorded.</td><td data-label="When it dreams">Nightly cron, 03:00 by default.</td><td data-label="What the dream does">Light: stage candidates. REM: themes, no durable write. Deep: three numeric gates (score, recall count, distinct queries), then the model picks add, merge or supersede.</td><td data-label="Where it writes">In place, MEMORY.md; a diary in DREAMS.md.</td><td data-label="Safeguards">Model returns operations, not prose; cap on how many old entries may be lost; source reference required; copy of the old file kept; untrusted sources excluded.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><a class="emblem-link" href="https://www.letta.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Letta website"><svg class="emblem" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="22" cy="22" r="8" fill="#f6f1e6" stroke="#b6aa92"/><path d="M10 52 Q22 32 34 52 Z" fill="#f6f1e6" stroke="#b6aa92"/><circle cx="44" cy="24" r="7" fill="#fffaf0" stroke="#a8843f"/><path d="M33 52 Q44 34 55 52 Z" fill="#fffaf0" stroke="#a8843f"/></svg></a><span class="name">Letta</span><span class="kind">CURATION</span></th><td data-label="Day writer">The main agent updates memory when it learns something durable; /remember.</td><td data-label="When it dreams">After a set number of agent steps, or when the context is compacted.</td><td data-label="What the dream does">Background subagents review recent conversations and update memory.</td><td data-label="Where it writes">In place.</td><td data-label="Safeguards">Optional second agent reviews the proposed changes; no human approval.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="note" style="margin-top:10px">More systems coming soon.</p>
</section>

